Article:
- This study used learner satisfaction as the dependent variable, which meant that its measure of success was the degree of satisfaction that students got from the course
- Having learner satisfaction is important to educational institutions because having satisfied students brings more students as they are more likely to recommend the institution to others and come back for more MOOCs
- Completion rate doesn’t take into account the diverse goals of MOOC students which are not the same as a normal college course
- This study adds to the field by identifying which attributes of MOOCs affect learner satisfaction
- Learners who completed courses had highest satisfaction and learners who dropped courses had lowest satisfaction

